WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.508
$6.7M Lesson.

2
00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:08.197
Nine deals. Six point seven million
dollars. Almost none of them made it to

3
00:00:08.197 --> 00:00:09.196
underwriting.

4
00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:14.665
These were real deals from our pipeline.
We're not disclosing company names. Each

5
00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:20.203
one was identified as a non-fit before it
reached the underwriting team. Every one

6
00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:25.399
maps back to the financial concepts we
just covered, or to a basic qualifying

7
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:27.587
question asked during discovery.

8
00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:32.845
You're never going to do as thorough a
job as the underwriting team — that's not

9
00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:37.571
your role. But you can catch the obvious
signs. Let's walk through four.

10
00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:42.481
A health and wellness company. This
company had recently gone through

11
00:00:42.481 --> 00:00:47.608
bankruptcy. They disclosed it on the
first call. When a company has been

12
00:00:47.608 --> 00:00:52.518
through bankruptcy, cash runway is
effectively zero and the net asset

13
00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:58.150
position is deeply negative. That's a
clear signal the deal isn't going to be a

14
00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.305
fit for Dash-fi.

15
00:00:59.305 --> 00:01:04.894
A connected home device company. This
company is wholly owned by a major tech

16
00:01:04.894 --> 00:01:10.483
conglomerate. They don't control their
own balance sheet, treasury, or credit

17
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:16.219
decisions. The parent company runs its
own card programs and therefore wasn't a

18
00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:21.809
fit. The corporate structure question —
"Is there a parent company or holding

19
00:01:21.809 --> 00:01:25.265
entity?" — would have surfaced this
immediately.

20
00:01:25.265 --> 00:01:31.465
A marketplace reseller. This company buys
products from third-party retailers and

21
00:01:31.465 --> 00:01:37.200
resells them on Amazon. It's an arbitrage
model — buy low, list higher on a

22
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.168
marketplace. The margins are razor thin.
A reseller's margin structure doesn't

23
00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:49.290
support the kind of credit extension we
offer. The business model didn't fit our

24
00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:49.600
ICP.

25
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.909
A young medical company. This company was
founded three years ago. The debt ratio

26
00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:59.886
was too high, and the cash position was
too small to support the limits they

27
00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:04.930
needed. A company that young, carrying
that much debt relative to its assets,

28
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.907
with that little cash in the bank — the
financial profile tells you it's not

29
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:12.495
ready. That's the balance sheet screen.

30
00:02:12.495 --> 00:02:17.684
Four deals. Four obvious signs —
financial distress, corporate structure,

31
00:02:17.684 --> 00:02:23.089
business model, and company maturity.
Bankruptcy means zero runway. A parent

32
00:02:23.089 --> 00:02:28.350
company means someone else controls the
balance sheet. Razor-thin reseller

33
00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:33.971
margins mean the business model doesn't
support our terms. And a company that's

34
00:02:33.971 --> 00:02:39.376
too young with too much debt and too
little cash isn't ready for passing our

35
00:02:39.376 --> 00:02:40.313
underwriting.

36
00:02:40.313 --> 00:02:45.403
The underwriting team is there for the
calls that require real evaluation. These

37
00:02:45.403 --> 00:02:50.107
weren't those calls. These were the ones
you can spot in the first fifteen

38
00:02:50.107 --> 00:02:50.622
minutes.

39
00:02:50.622 --> 00:02:56.447
That wraps Module 0. You now have the
financial vocabulary, the underwriting

40
00:02:56.447 --> 00:03:02.117
team's evaluation framework, and the
pattern of what goes wrong when these

41
00:03:02.117 --> 00:03:04.136
questions don't get asked.

42
00:03:04.136 --> 00:03:08.984
Let's move on to Module 1 takes you
inside the discovery process, how to

43
00:03:08.984 --> 00:03:14.242
handle objections against our application
requirements and how to prepare your

44
00:03:14.242 --> 00:03:17.929
